  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Private Enterprises for the Digital Economy (SPEED)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Philippines):  .USAID, through the SPEED activity, will expand the participation of Philippine small and medium enterprises (SMEs) in the digital economy. USAID will work with the government and private sector to mobilize resources in the digital economy for enterprise-led growth. FY 2022 funds will support initiatives that will build the foundation for SME transition to the digital economy and push the country&apos;s digitalization agenda forward. These include technical assistance support for priority e-commerce policies such as the E-Commerce Roadmap 2028, e-Commerce Act, and the Internet Transactions Act. USAID will convene industry players to identify the challenges and co-create innovative solutions to increase e-payments use among SMEs and develop an interoperable logistics and payments network. USAID will work with government agencies on policies aimed at improving SME and customer trust and confidence on digital platforms. USAID will develop targeted training programs for SMEs and matching programs between technology companies and start-ups to accelerate their digital transformation. ..USAID will support the shift towards a circular economy and greener e-commerce sector by helping implement interventions that will reduce the use of plastics, including the use of more eco-friendly materials and sustainable processes. These interventions aim to reduce environmental impact of the logistics sector - covering the entire product life cycle from sourcing, manufacturing, warehousing, transport, marketing and use and disposal of plastics packaging. USAID will work with the Philippine government and the private sector to improve the efficiency of the logistics chain by optimizing distribution network and routes and increasing the use of pick-up points in both urban and rural areas, recycling or repurposing returned or end of life goods thereby enhancing reverse logistics systems, and promoting consumer awareness on the environmental impact of excessive packaging.  .. ..</narrative>
  </description>
